Privacy Policy for tomomai

Effective Date: December 2, 2025

This Privacy Policy describes how shedaniel ("Developer," "I," or "we"), the operator of the open-source project tomomai, collects, uses, stores, and protects personal data from users in Hong Kong and internationally.

1. Data Controller Contact Information

- Data Controller: shedaniel
- Location: Hong Kong Special Administrative Region
- Legal Contact for Data Requests: daniel@shedaniel.me

2. Data We Collect and How We Collect It

We collect two main categories of data, which are necessary for the Service's function:

Identity/Login Data
- Elements Collected: Discord username, profile picture, email address.
- Source: Via Discord OAuth2 login.
- Purpose: Account creation, identification, and communication.

Third-Party Data (Sensitive)
- Elements Collected: maimai DX NET login details/cookies, User ID, game scores, performance records, achievements.
- Source: Directly from the user, used to scrape data from maimai DX NET (SEGA) on the user's behalf.
- Purpose: To provide the core functionality of the Service (displaying game data).

Operational Data
- Elements Collected: IP addresses, request times, pages accessed.
- Source: Vercel logs (our hosting provider).
- Purpose: Service monitoring, security, debugging, and traffic analysis.

3. Basis and Use of Your Personal Data

Under the Hong Kong Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (PDPO), we process your data based on Consent and Legitimate Interests.

Cookies and Local Storage
We use session cookies and/or local storage to maintain your login session and preferences (including authentication and language settings). These are "essential" for the Service to function. We do not use cookies for third-party tracking or advertising.

Consent
- Usage: Using your maimai DX NET credentials to scrape and display your game data. By logging in and providing these details, you explicitly consent to this processing.

Legitimate Interest
- Usage: Operational data (Vercel logs) is processed to maintain service security, stability, and troubleshoot issues.

Specific Data Uses:

- Service Delivery: To fetch, store, and display your personal maimai DX NET statistics.
- User Profiles (Optional Public Setting): Users may voluntarily set their profile to public. This action makes their tomomai profile visible to anyone and may be indexed by public search engines (e.g., Google, Bing).
- Aggregation: We use scraped data to generate aggregated and anonymized statistics (e.g., total number of songs played across all users). This aggregated data is publicly available on the website and does not contain any personally identifiable information.

4. Data Storage and Security

4.1 Security Measures
We take reasonable steps to protect the personal data we hold. Specifically, the sensitive maimai DX NET login details/cookies are protected using AES-256-GCM encryption. This is an industry-standard encryption protocol.

However, you acknowledge that no method of transmission over the Internet or method of electronic storage is 100% secure. You provide your data at your own risk.

In the unlikely event of a data breach that compromises your personal data, we will notify you via the email address associated with your account in accordance with applicable laws.

4.2 Data Retention
We retain all collected personal data, including Discord data and scraped maimai DX NET data, indefinitely, or until you request its deletion. This allows you to maintain your full performance history on the Service.

5. Sharing of Personal Data

We do not share identifiable personal data with third parties for marketing or other commercial purposes.

The only instances of data disclosure are:

- Service Providers: We use Vercel for hosting, which processes operational data (logs).
- Public Profiles: If you opt-in to make your profile public, that data is shared with the public, including search engines.
- Legal Compliance: If required by law, court order, or governmental regulation in Hong Kong or another applicable jurisdiction.

6. Your Rights (Data Access and Deletion)

As a user, you have rights regarding your personal data under the PDPO. You have the right to:

1. Request Access: Obtain a copy of your personal data we hold (Data Takeout).
2. Request Correction: Request the correction of any inaccurate data. (Note: Most data is scraped from SEGA, so primary corrections should be made there).
3. Request Erasure (Deletion): Request the permanent deletion of your account and all associated data.

All requests for data access or deletion must be submitted via email to: daniel@shedaniel.me. We will respond to your request within the time frames required by Hong Kong law.

7. Notice to Users in the European Economic Area (EEA)

If you are a resident of the EEA, you have additional rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

Legal Basis for Processing
We process your personal data based on the following legal grounds:
- Consent: When you choose to log in and link your maimai DX NET account.
- Legitimate Interests: For ensuring the security and operational integrity of our Service (e.g., server logs).

Your GDPR Rights
In addition to the rights listed in Section 6 (which include the right to access/port your data and withdraw consent via account deletion), you also have the right to:
- Restrict Processing: Request that we limit the processing of your personal data.
- Object to Processing: Object to our processing of your data based on legitimate interests.
- Lodge a Complaint: You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority in your country of residence if you believe we have violated your data protection rights.

International Transfers
Your personal data is processed in Hong Kong and on servers controlled by our service providers (e.g., Vercel) which are primarily located in Japan or other jurisdictions. By using the Service, you acknowledge and consent to the transfer of your data outside the EEA to countries that may not offer the same level of data protection as your home country.

8. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. We will notify you of any material changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Effective Date" at the top.
